From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:05:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Restyle less on each change

Add a style-only resolve for computed-value readers: resolve_style runs the inputs
the cascade needs and the stylist and leaves restyle damage on the nodes for the
next full resolve, reporting false when a query container exists because @container
rules cascade against laid-out sizes. Whether a query container exists is a sticky
flag that the style traversal and the full-resolve container snapshot set.

Restyle only structurally affected siblings on child insertion: like Gecko's
RestyleForInsertOrChange, restyle the inserted children and use the parent's
selector flags to restyle only the edge children or later siblings that structural
selectors can match. :empty, from-end selectors, sibling-index(), slots and shadow
hosts keep the whole-parent restyle, and :has() keeps its own invalidator.

Cache parsed query selectors and hint sibling indexes: a small thread-local hint
per parent slot, always checked against the list, makes in-order sibling steps
constant time without growing Node.

Reshape only text that names a newly registered web font family, and the inline
roots above it, since only that text can shape differently; a face with no family
name still reshapes everything. The damage is applied at the next resolve rather
than on each delivery, so a page that receives N faces walks its nodes once instead
of N times.
